TITLE:: SPSnapshot
summary:: the node tree at one moment, two of them compared, one written to disk
categories:: Libraries>ServerPanel
related:: Classes/SPTree, Classes/SPRouting

DESCRIPTION::
A snapshot is an link::Classes/Event::: the tree with every synth's controls, the names of its groups and synths, the busses with their writers, readers and levels, the problems, the paused synths, the time. link::Classes/SPTree#-snapshot:: makes them; this class compares two, writes one as text, and saves and loads them. Language only.

code::
s.boot;
t = SPTree(s);
t.snapshot;                               // made from the server's next answer
x = { SinOsc.ar(300) * 0.05 }.play;
t.snapshot;
SPSnapshot.diff(t.snapshots[1], t.snapshots[0]).do { |c| [c[\kind], c[\text]].postln };
SPSnapshot.text(t.snapshots[0]).postln;
x.free;
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: make
A snapshot of a tree. SPTree calls this.
ARGUMENT:: server
The link::Classes/Server::.
ARGUMENT:: tree
The root node Event.
ARGUMENT:: labels
Group names by id.
ARGUMENT:: names
What each synth is, by id.
ARGUMENT:: model
link::Classes/SPRouting::'s.
ARGUMENT:: levels
Bus levels by channel.
ARGUMENT:: problems
As SPTree lists them.
ARGUMENT:: paused
The ids of the paused synths.

METHOD:: diff
What changed from one snapshot to another: nodes added and removed (several synths of one def in one group are one line), nodes that moved, controls that changed, busses whose writers or readers are other SynthDefs or that went from sounding to silent, problems that came or went.
ARGUMENT:: a
The earlier snapshot.
ARGUMENT:: b
The later one.
RETURNS:: an Array of Events code::(kind:, id:, text:)::, code::kind:: one of code::\added \removed \moved \control \bus \problem::

METHOD:: text
A snapshot as a page of text: the tree in the server's order with every control, the busses, the problems.
ARGUMENT:: snap
A snapshot.

METHOD:: title
One line: its time and how many nodes.
ARGUMENT:: snap
A snapshot.

METHOD:: counts
code::[groups, synths]::.
ARGUMENT:: snap
A snapshot.

METHOD:: index
Its nodes by id, and the ids in tree order.
ARGUMENT:: snap
A snapshot.
RETURNS:: code::[an IdentityDictionary, an Array]::

METHOD:: save
Write a snapshot as code::tree-<stamp>.snapshot:: (an archive) and code::tree-<stamp>.txt::.
ARGUMENT:: snap
A snapshot.
ARGUMENT:: dir
A folder; link::#*folder:: when nil.
RETURNS:: the archive's path

METHOD:: load
Read an archive back.
ARGUMENT:: path
A code::.snapshot:: file.

METHOD:: files
The archives in a folder, newest first.
ARGUMENT:: dir
A folder; link::#*folder:: when nil.

METHOD:: folder
Where snapshots and logs are written: code::server-panel-snapshots:: in the user support directory. Set it to write elsewhere.

METHOD:: copyTree
A node and everything under it, copied.
ARGUMENT:: node
A node Event.

METHOD:: nameOf
A node of a snapshot in words.
ARGUMENT:: snap
A snapshot.
ARGUMENT:: node
One of its nodes.

METHOD:: pathText
The groups above a node, by name.
ARGUMENT:: snap
A snapshot.
ARGUMENT:: node
One of its nodes.

METHOD:: db
A level in words.
ARGUMENT:: amp
An amplitude, or nil.
